# Chroma library, modern Earth: the commerce sphere's events as they touch a life (Library thread, 2026-10-09, "v22"
# update stage 4, item 15 phase 3). Design: chroma-ideas/spheres-implementation.md sections 2, 4 "Library" and 5; data:
# chroma-ideas/spheres-data/comm.json (events with on_character and the modern epoch; each scene is built on the event's
# wording.modern and on_character). Face words: chroma-library/earth_spheres.py (Fair measure, Careful reckoning, Shrewd
# bargain, Haggle and dare, Gift and return). Fields: build.py (the spheres' fields of world-fields.md, 2026-10-09).
#
# Commerce is the market, the shop and credit: prices, debts, loans, stalls, wages and gifts. No currency, brand, bank
# or company is named; money is "the wage", "the pot", "a month's pay".
#
# Every moment here is an event moment: a life event the Engine fires on its sphere event (sphere_event: <key>) for the
# people its selector names (place, members or all); per_year is all 0 and there are no drivers. The '# world:' line
# above each moment gives the event key, the selector and the share of selected people who meet the moment (estimate).
# Twenty moments, one per comm event that has on_character and a modern wording (hoard_shamed, usury_banned,
# match_gifts, gift_partner_comes and seed_lent have no modern wording). Tone follows the event's tone (good = joy,
# bad = trouble, mixed = mixed): 6 joy, 7 trouble, 7 mixed.
#
# Next to earth.py: 'a crash takes the savings' holds the savings lost in a crash, so lender_fails here is the loan
# called in; 'money worries end' is a debt paid off by one's own hand, so debts_forgiven is the relief law; 'losing the
# home' is the eviction, so rents_jump is the rise at renewal; 'the skip outside the old shop' is the closing itself,
# so big_store is the store's coming; 'a recession' and 'a boom year' are the whole economy, so coin_debased and mania
# are one price each (money, houses).
#
# Options: sphere: on each is the face the act is in (one-colour X: comm.X; a pair: its pair face in wheel order, so
# WR is comm.RW, WG comm.GW, UG comm.GU). Levers (lever:) where the act plainly is one, from character.levers.
#
# Layout: each a life event with the five one-colour options and one pair set. The twenty use all twelve halves of D1 to
# D6, eight of them twice (D1b, D2a, D3a, D3b, D4b, D5b, D6a, D6b), each chosen to hold the event's own pair faces
# where it has them (the pawn lender BG, the family banker WB, the boycott leader RW).
# Evenness: in every moment each colour's one-colour chance plus half its two pairs' chances is the same sum, so every
# colour has the same mean chance in each moment and in every stage. No flags.
#
# share: and once: on every moment (2026-10-10, Engine phase 3c): the engine draws at birth who can ever meet the
# moment (share:), and they meet it at most once (once: yes). Shares are the '# world:' share times .5, so the 157
# moments together come to about 13 a life at the fitted event rates (Engine table chroma-engine/notes/sphev-per-moment.tsv:
# 92 a life before). The '# world:' line keeps the share of the people an event reaches, as written.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- lender_fails (pairs D6a)

# world: sphere event lender_fails, selector place, share .25
== the loan the new owners call in
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: lender_fails
share: 0.13
once: yes
haunt: comm.credit
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 20-85
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: lender_fails (sphere comm). Selector place: a lender holding many of the town's debts fails after years of fast credit; about 1 in 4 people in the town have a loan called in, savings frozen or hours cut because of it (share .25, estimate), once in a life for most who meet it (estimate)
likelier: a town that borrowed heavily in good years, one big local lender, a loan for a business, a van or a roof
rarer: no debts, savings spread over safe places, a town served by many lenders
tone: trouble
life: money, work, home
horizon: months
roles: parent, boss, neighbour
earth: the bank that held the town's loans collapses, and the firm that buys its books calls in your loan
scene: The bank that held half the town's loans has collapsed. The firm that bought its books writes that {Ns} loan must be repaid within ninety days, and at work {boss} is cutting everyone's hours.
scene W: {N} signed for that loan and means to honour it. The question is how, and whom else {N} owes first.
scene U: The letter quotes a clause {N} has never read. Somewhere in the small print there may be more time.
scene B: Other lenders are already circling the old bank's customers. Someone will offer better terms, at a price.
scene R: Ninety days. {N} would rather sell everything and start from nothing than spend three months begging.
scene G: {Ns} family lent half the street money in the hard years. {N} knows whom to ask, and who will ask back.
- W | write to everyone you owe and set out an honest plan to pay each in turn | v: conformity, security | sphere: comm.W | chance: 77
- U | read the loan papers clause by clause, and find what the new owners can really demand | v: self-direction, security | sphere: comm.U | chance: 66
- B | move the loan to a rival lender before the deadline, at a higher rate | v: power, security | lever: exit | pushes: institution | sphere: comm.B | chance: 56
- R | sell the van and the tools, clear the debt, and start again small | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | sphere: comm.R | chance: 80
- G | ask your parents for a loan, as they once asked theirs | v: tradition, security | sphere: comm.G | chance: 48
- BG | take the good watch to the pawn shop to see the month through | v: security | sphere: comm.BG | chance: 80
- UG | sit the family down and draw up a household budget everyone keeps to | v: security, tradition | sphere: comm.GU | chance: 66
- UR | start a small trade from the spare room, planned to cover the payments | v: self-direction, achievement | lever: found | sphere: comm.UR | chance: 44
- WB | lend a neighbour the money to keep their shop open, on written terms | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | sphere: comm.WB | chance: 50
- WR | march with the other borrowers to the council to demand time to pay | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: comm.RW | chance: 38
works: The new owners accept a plan, and the loan is paid off two years later than it should have been, but paid.
works: {N} comes through the winter with less, and with a clear idea of who stood by them.
fails: The ninety days run out, and the next letter is from the bailiffs.
fails: {N} gets through the deadline, but the hours never come back, and the debt follows them for years.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- new_route (pairs D2a)

# world: sphere event new_route, selector place, share .3
== the depot at the edge of town
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: new_route
share: 0.15
once: yes
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature
age: 16-70
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: new_route (sphere comm). Selector place: a new road, rail line or depot brings far goods and trade within reach of a town that has something to sell; about 3 in 10 of its people feel it as new work, new goods or a trade that loses out (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a town of working age, a trade that can ship its goods, a shop on the old road
rarer: a remote place the route passes by, a person retired or settled in one trade
tone: joy
life: work, money, community
horizon: months
roles: parent, friend
earth: a new highway and a freight depot open at the edge of town, trucks come at all hours, and jobs come with them
scene: A new highway and a freight depot have opened at the edge of town. Trucks come and go at all hours, the depot is hiring, and the shops on the old road have lost half their passing trade.
scene W: The depot hires through the job centre, with a written wage and a list. {N} likes work that is open to anyone.
scene U: Goods that took a week to reach the town now come overnight. {N} is working out what could now go the other way.
scene B: Every driver who stops needs fuel, a meal and a bed. {N} has noticed the empty plot by the slip road.
scene R: The trucks go everywhere {N} has never been, and the depot wants drivers for the long runs.
scene G: {Ns} family has kept the shop on the old road for two generations. The trucks no longer pass its door.
- W | apply for a depot job through the job centre, like everyone else | v: conformity, security | sphere: comm.W | chance: 60
- U | work out what the town makes that could now sell far away, and tell the council | v: universalism, achievement | sphere: comm.U | chance: 73
- B | rent the empty plot by the slip road and open a food van for drivers | v: achievement, power | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: comm.B | chance: 60
- R | train for a heavy goods licence and take the long-distance runs | v: stimulation, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | sphere: comm.R | chance: 72
- G | keep the family shop on the old road open for the neighbours who still come | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | pushes: place | sphere: comm.G | chance: 51
- BG | open the family shop late for the night shift at the depot | v: achievement, tradition | sphere: comm.BG | chance: 70
- BR | buy goods off the trucks in bulk and sell them at the weekend market | v: achievement, stimulation | sphere: comm.BR | chance: 54
- UR | start a small delivery round linking the depot to the villages | v: self-direction, achievement | lever: found | sphere: comm.UR | chance: 46
- WG | help the strangers who came for depot work find rooms and a doctor | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: comm.GW | chance: 72
- WU | ask the council for safe crossings on the depot road before someone is hurt | v: universalism, security | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: comm.WU | chance: 52
works: The depot brings steady wages, and {N} finds a place in the town's new shape.
works: A year on, the trucks are part of the town's sound, and {N} is better off for them.
fails: The jobs go to people from elsewhere, and the town gets the noise without the wages.
fails: {N} backs the old road or the new one, and the bet does not pay.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- market_granted (pairs D5b)

# world: sphere event market_granted, selector place, share .3
== the market in the empty car park
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: market_granted
share: 0.15
once: yes
haunt: comm.market
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 13-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: market_granted (sphere comm). Selector place: a council grants a regular market day in a town with enough people and safe streets; about 3 in 10 residents make it part of their week, as buyers or with a stall (share .3, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a town centre with empty space, a person who makes or grows something, free Saturday mornings
rarer: a town with many shops already, long weekend shifts, poor health
tone: joy
life: money, community, friends
horizon: months
roles: grandparent, friend
earth: the council opens a weekly market in the empty car park, and a pitch costs little
scene: The council has opened a weekly market in the empty car park. By eight on Saturday the growers, bakers and second-hand sellers are set up, and a pitch costs less than a night out.
scene W: The market warden gives pitches by turn and checks the scales in the open. {N} likes a place where the rules are posted.
scene U: {N} walks every row before buying anything, and already knows whose eggs are cheapest and whose bread is best.
scene B: A pitch costs little. {N} wonders what a stall of their own could earn in a year of Saturdays.
scene R: The noise, the calling of prices, the haggling over an old lamp. {N} has not enjoyed a Saturday morning so much in years.
scene G: Half the street is here, talking over the stalls. {grandparent} says it is like the market of their youth.
- W | help the market warden check the scales and give the pitches out by turn | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: comm.W | chance: 78
- U | walk every row before buying, and keep a list of the best prices | v: self-direction, security | sphere: comm.U | chance: 74
- B | take a pitch of your own and sell what you make | v: achievement, self-direction | lever: found | pushes: place | sphere: comm.B | chance: 83
- R | haggle for the oldest lamp on the second-hand stall, just for the fun of it | v: hedonism, stimulation | sphere: comm.R | chance: 69
- G | buy from the same growers every week and learn their children's names | v: tradition, benevolence | lever: loyalty | sphere: comm.G | chance: 66
- BR | buy at house clearances and sell at the market with a patter of your own | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: comm.BR | chance: 56
- RG | bring the whole family to spend Saturday morning at the market | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: comm.RG | chance: 82
- UG | start a stall swapping seeds and cuttings from neighbours' gardens | v: tradition, universalism | sphere: comm.GU | chance: 62
- WB | lend a young grower the money for a first pitch, repaid from the sales | v: benevolence, power | lever: fund | sphere: comm.WB | chance: 54
- WU | help write the market's rules so that every pitch is given by turn | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: comm.WU | chance: 66
works: The market grows into the town's Saturday, and {N} has a place in it.
works: By autumn {N} knows half the stallholders by name, and the car park is never empty.
fails: The market is busy for one summer, then thins, and the council talks of selling the car park.
fails: {N} spends more than planned and earns less, and the Saturdays lose their shine.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- dearth (pairs D3a)

# world: sphere event dearth, selector place, share .5
== the weekly shop buys less each month
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: dearth
share: 0.25
once: yes
haunt: comm.shop
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-30
times: World event: dearth (sphere comm). Selector place: food grows dear after a lean year, a fuel shock or a blockade (the world's food price shock maps onto it, spheres-implementation section 5); about half of the households in the place feel it as cut meals, a tab or something sold (share .5, estimate), a few times in a life (estimate)
likelier: a low or single wage, children at home, a pension, a town far from cheap shops
rarer: a good income, a garden or a farm, savings to ride out the season
tone: trouble
life: money, home, family
horizon: months
roles: child, parent, neighbour
earth: fuel and a poor harvest push food prices up every month, and the queue at the food bank reaches the corner
scene: Fuel costs have jumped on top of a poor harvest. Food prices rise every month, {Ns} weekly shop buys less than it did, and the food bank's queue now reaches the corner.
scene W: {N} has always paid the shop on time. This month the money will not cover what the household needs.
scene U: {N} has started writing down every price, every week. Something has to give, and the figures will show what.
scene B: The shelves empty a little more each week, and some shops are holding stock back. Whoever buys before the next rise comes out ahead.
scene R: {N} is sick of counting coins at the till. There must be cheaper food somewhere, for someone quick enough.
scene G: Nobody on the street admits to going short. {N} knows which neighbours have stopped buying meat.
- W | share out what there is fairly, and cut your own plate first | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: comm.W | chance: 84
- U | plan a month of meals by price, and keep to the list | v: security, self-direction | sphere: comm.U | chance: 64
- B | buy dried goods in bulk now, before the next rise | v: security, power | sphere: comm.B | chance: 61
- R | haggle at the market at closing time for whatever the stalls have left | v: stimulation, security | sphere: comm.R | chance: 84
- G | run a tab at the corner shop whose owner has known your family for years | v: tradition, security | sphere: comm.G | chance: 63
- BG | sell the good bicycle to keep the cupboards full until spring | v: security | sphere: comm.BG | chance: 78
- RG | cook one big pot each Sunday with the neighbours, everyone bringing what they can | v: benevolence, hedonism | sphere: comm.RG | chance: 72
- UB | compare every shop's prices and buy each thing where it is cheapest | v: security, achievement | sphere: comm.UB | chance: 76
- WR | join the neighbours demanding that the council cap the price of bread | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: comm.RW | chance: 36
- WU | help the food bank set up a fair rota so everyone in the queue is served | v: benevolence, universalism | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: comm.WU | chance: 72
works: The household eats plainer for a season, but nobody goes without, and prices ease by the next harvest.
works: {N} gets through the dear months, and the neighbours who shared with them are closer for it.
fails: The tab grows faster than the wage, and the debt at the shop outlasts the dear months.
fails: {N} keeps the cupboards full, but something sold that winter can never be bought back.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- crowd_price (pairs D4b)

# world: sphere event crowd_price, selector place, share .4
== the shop that tripled the price of water
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: crowd_price
share: 0.2
once: yes
haunt: comm.shop
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 15-40
times: World event: crowd_price (sphere comm). Selector place: in dear times a seller is seen holding back stock or raising a price beyond what neighbours think just, and the crowd acts; about 4 in 10 people in the place join, keep away, help the seller or report it (share .4, estimate), once or twice in a life (estimate)
likelier: a storm or shortage, one shop serving a neighbourhood, a close street with a sense of what is fair
rarer: many shops to choose from, plentiful stock, a street where neighbours seldom meet
tone: mixed
life: community, money, conflict
horizon: week
roles: friend, neighbour
earth: after the storm a shop triples the price of bottled water, the neighbours picket it, and the council caps prices for a month
scene: After the storm the mains water is off, and the shop on the corner has tripled the price of bottled water. Neighbours are picketing its door, and the owner, whom {N} has known for years, is shouting back.
scene W: A fair price is a fair price, storm or no storm. {N} wants the council to set one for everyone.
scene U: {N} wonders what the owner paid for the water, and whether the stock will last the week at any price.
scene B: Water sells at three times the price because people need it. {N} sees the sense in that, and the danger.
scene R: The crowd is loud and getting louder. {N} feels the anger rising, and wants a placard.
scene G: The owner gave {Ns} family credit through a hard winter years ago. Now the neighbours are calling him a thief.
- W | report the price to the council and ask for a cap on water | v: universalism, conformity | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: comm.W | chance: 78
- U | find out what the shop paid for the water, and post the figures for the street | v: universalism, self-direction | sphere: comm.U | chance: 68
- B | fetch water by the pallet from the next town, and sell it at a fair margin | v: achievement, power | sphere: comm.B | chance: 68
- R | join the picket at the door and lead the chanting | v: stimulation, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: comm.R | chance: 67
- G | share the water you stored with the neighbours on your stairs | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: comm.G | chance: 74
- BR | sell cheap water by the picket from the boot of your car | v: stimulation, achievement | sphere: comm.BR | chance: 62
- UB | quietly ask the owner to drop the price before the council does it for him | v: security, power | sphere: comm.UB | chance: 52
- UG | get the street collecting rainwater and sharing it house by house | v: benevolence, security | sphere: comm.GU | chance: 62
- WG | stand between the owner and the crowd and ask both sides to calm down | v: security, benevolence | sphere: comm.GW | chance: 40
- WR | lead a boycott of the shop until the price comes down | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: place | sphere: comm.RW | chance: 54
works: The council caps the price for a month, the water comes back, and the street remembers who stood with it.
works: The owner backs down by evening, and within a week both sides are buying and selling as before.
fails: The shop closes for good, and the street loses the only grocer within walking distance.
fails: The picket turns sour, a window is broken in the night, and {N} is caught in the middle of the blame.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- debts_forgiven (pairs D1b)

# world: sphere event debts_forgiven, selector all, share .15
== the letter that writes off the debt
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: debts_forgiven
share: 0.08
once: yes
haunt: comm.credit
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-95
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 20-60
times: World event: debts_forgiven (sphere comm). Selector all: a relief law caps old debts and writes off the smallest, after unrest, a crisis or a new government; about 15 in 100 adults hold a debt it reaches, or a loan they made that it cancels (share .15, estimate), seldom more than once in a life (estimate)
likelier: old debts from a hard year, a low income, a family that borrows from lenders rather than kin
rarer: no debts, a large mortgage the law does not reach, a calm economy
tone: joy
life: money, home, family
horizon: years
roles: sibling, friend
earth: a relief law caps old debts and writes off the smallest, and the letter says yours is gone
scene: A new relief law caps old debts and writes off the smallest. {N} opens the letter at the kitchen table: the debt that has shaped six years is gone, and the year can start over.
scene W: {N} borrowed that money and always meant to pay it back. A law has cleared the debt, but some promises were {Ns} own.
scene U: Without the monthly payment, a fifth of the wage is free. {N} is already working out what it can do.
scene B: Clean books, and lenders who will lend again. {N} sees the chance to borrow for something that pays.
scene R: Six years of dreading the post, and it is over. {N} wants to shout it from the window.
scene G: {sibling} is still paying a debt the law did not reach. {N} thinks of them first.
- W | pay back the friend who lent you money in the bad years, though no law asks | v: benevolence, conformity | mark: kept your word | sphere: comm.W | chance: 72
- U | put the freed money aside each month until there is a year's cushion | v: security | sphere: comm.U | chance: 73
- B | borrow on the clean record to buy the van the business needs | v: achievement, power | sphere: comm.B | chance: 77
- R | throw a party for everyone who helped you through the debt years | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: comm.R | chance: 67
- G | sit with your brother or sister over their own letters, to see if their debt qualifies | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | sphere: comm.G | chance: 57
- RG | take the family away on the first holiday in six years | v: hedonism, benevolence | sphere: comm.RG | chance: 76
- UB | read the new law closely and find which of your other debts it caps | v: security, power | sphere: comm.UB | chance: 64
- UR | spend the first free months learning the trade you put off in the debt years | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | sphere: comm.UR | chance: 54
- WB | set up a small fund at work that lends colleagues money without interest | v: benevolence, power | lever: found | sphere: comm.WB | chance: 46
- WG | volunteer at the advice centre, helping neighbours read their own letters | v: benevolence, universalism | sphere: comm.GW | chance: 74
works: The first year without the debt is the best {N} has had in a long time, and the habits of the hard years stay.
works: {N} uses the fresh start well, and the money that went to the lender now builds something.
fails: Within two years a new debt has crept into the place the old one left.
fails: The relief comes too late for {sibling}, and the family's joy is uneven.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- licences_few (pairs D1a)

# world: sphere event licences_few, selector members, share .7
== a ten-year wait for a permit
tier: life event
sphere: comm
sphere_event: licences_few
share: 0.36
once: yes
haunt: comm.market
ladder: known
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-80
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
gap: 10-40
times: World event: licences_few (sphere comm). Selector members: the council or the trade caps stalls, licences or permits in hard or crowded times; about 7 in 10 of the street sellers and stallholders without one must pay, partner an insider, sell without, or leave (share .7, estimate), once or twice in a trading life (estimate)
likelier: a crowded trade, a stall without a permit, a city that favours shops over streets
rarer: an old permit already held, a quiet town with free pitches, a trade done indoors
tone: trouble
life: work, money, law
horizon: years
roles: parent, rival
earth: the city caps street-vendor permits with a ten-year waiting list, and your stall has none
scene: The city has capped street-vendor permits, with a ten-year waiting list. {Ns} stall has stood on the same corner for years without one, and the inspectors have started handing out fines.
scene W: {N} would gladly pay for a permit and keep every rule. There are simply no permits to be had.
scene U: The new rule runs to forty pages. {N} suspects there is a gap in it somewhere, for anyone who reads closely.
scene B: {rival} holds three permits from the old days and rents them out by the month. {N} could pay, or find another way.
scene R: Ten years! {N} has a stall to run this week, and the inspectors cannot be everywhere.
scene G: {N} learned the trade at {parent}'s side, on this same corner. The regulars know the stall, permit or no permit.
- W | put your name on the waiting list and sell only where no permit is needed | v: conformity, security | sphere: comm.W | chance: 74
- U | read the new rule closely and find the pitches it does not cover | v: self-direction, security | sphere: comm.U | chance: 71
- B | rent a spare permit from an old holder, at whatever price they ask | v: achievement, security | sphere: comm.B | chance: 56
- R | keep selling on the corner, and pack up fast when the inspectors come | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: broke the law | lever: subvert | sphere: comm.R | chance: 67
- G | move the stall to the family's front yard, where the neighbours can find it | v: tradition, security | sphere: comm.G | chance: 62
- BG | go into partnership with a cousin who holds a permit, and share the takings | v: security, tradition | sphere: comm.BG | chance: 62
- BR | pay a shopkeeper for the use of their doorway, which the rule allows | v: achievement, self-direction | sphere: comm.BR | chance: 58
- UG | gather the old vendors' records to prove the stalls were here long before the rule | v: tradition, universalism | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: comm.GU | chance: 46
- WR | march with the vendors on the city hall to open the permit rolls | v: universalism, self-direction | lever: voice | pushes: state | sphere: comm.RW | chance: 40
- WU | draft a scheme that gives permits out by turn, and take it to the council | v: universalism, conformity | sphere: comm.WU | chance: 44
works: The rolls open a little after the vendors' campaign, and {N} gets a permit years early.
works: {N} finds a lawful way to keep selling, and the regulars follow the stall.
fails: The fines pile up until the stall costs more than it earns.
fails: The inspectors take the cart, stock and all, and getting it back costs a month's takings.

