likelier: a high street with empty units, a town that newcomers move to, a shop of one's own nearby
rarer: a closed town few move to, a high street full of chain stores, a person who seldom shops locally
tone: mixed
life: community, money, work
horizon: years
roles: friend, neighbour
earth: the empty high street fills with shops run by families from abroad, and their children work the till after school
scene: The empty high street has filled with shops run by families from abroad: a bakery, a phone repair shop, a grocer open until midnight. Their children work the till after school, and one window has a card in it: help wanted.
scene W: Some on the street mutter about the newcomers. {N} thinks a shop that keeps fair prices deserves a fair welcome.
scene U: The new grocer stocks things nobody here sold before. {N} wonders where they come from, and how.
scene B: The new families work longer hours than anyone. {N} respects it, and sees the competition coming.
scene R: There is a bakery selling bread {N} has never tasted. {N} wants to try everything on the counter.
scene G: The old butcher closed last year, and his daughter moved away. {N} misses the old street, and is curious about the new one.
