scene: The market stalls now take payment by phone, and half of them have stopped taking cash at all. {grandparent} has always paid in coins from a purse, and today came home without the bread.
scene W: Paying should be open to everyone, phone or no phone. {N} thinks the stalls that refuse cash are leaving people out.
scene U: {N} has read how the phone payments work, and what they cost the stallholder on every sale.
scene B: The stallholders who switched first are selling faster. {N} sees which way the market is going.
scene R: One tap and it is done. {N} likes the speed of it, and the little sound it makes.
scene G: {grandparent} trusts only what can be held in the hand. {N} understands, more than they say.
