earth: the rent goes up by a fifth at renewal, and the family weighs a move an hour out
scene: The landlord's letter says the rent will rise by a fifth at renewal. A flat an hour out of town costs what this one does now, but the children would change schools, and {partner} would lose an hour each way.
scene W: {N} has paid the rent on the day for six years. A fifth more feels like a bargain broken.
scene U: {N} has the figures: rents up, wages flat, and the landlord's own costs barely changed.
scene B: Every landlord in town is doing the same. {N} wonders who is buying up the street, and what they want.
scene R: {N} is half tempted to pack up and go somewhere new altogether. Why stay and pay more?
scene G: {Ns} parents live two streets away, and all of {child}'s friends are on this street.
